WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.870
- [Mark] All right, Helia.

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:07.780
Helia, where'd you grow up?

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.171
Where are you from originally?

00:00:09.171 --> 00:00:11.473
- [Helia] I was born in
the Azores in Portugal.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:13.703
- [Mark] And where'd you grow up?

00:00:13.703 --> 00:00:16.573
- [Helia] I was brought up
in Lowell, Massachusetts.

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:19.723
- [Mark] Tell me about your childhood.

00:00:19.723 --> 00:00:21.920
You had both your parents as a kid?

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:23.460
- I was brought up by

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:27.420
my grandmother, grandfather,
until I was seven.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.540
And from seven to 16,

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.830
I stayed with my parents and got pregnant.

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:35.073
Went on my own.

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.740
Stayed in Massachusetts
til my son was nine

00:00:42.013 --> 00:00:44.563
and been out here the rest of the time.

00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:47.943
Now he's grown up.

00:00:51.222 --> 00:00:53.270
And I've been out here for 21 years

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:57.670
and didn't even call
my family for 20 years.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.870
They thought I was dead.

00:01:01.116 --> 00:01:03.150
And just time goes by really fast

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:05.930
when you're not doing right,

00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:10.770
and the number one reason
why homeless people

00:01:10.770 --> 00:01:13.793
don't contact their family
is because of shame.

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:16.763
And it was so wrong.

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:19.600
My grandparents are dead

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.000
and my mom and dad, they're
in their late eighties

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.230
they just went back to Portugal.

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.653
They came and visit me.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:31.003
I have five sisters, I'm the oldest.

00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.463
And it feels good to have
a family after so long.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.050
- [Mark] So you're still
in touch with everyone?

00:01:40.050 --> 00:01:42.180
- Yeah, I just talked to my sisters.

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:45.433
We all get together on the phone

00:01:46.949 --> 00:01:51.949
and they were coming to visit
me until this corona sickness.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.453
Now they just stay in the house.

00:01:57.240 --> 00:01:59.360
- [Mark] What is your drug today?

00:01:59.360 --> 00:02:01.750
- I smoke crack.

00:02:01.750 --> 00:02:03.183
- [Mark] And you've been
doing that since when?

00:02:04.270 --> 00:02:09.270
- Since I was 17.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.280
- [Mark] How'd you first
get turned onto crack?

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:18.280
- I started doing lines of
powder cocaine back East.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:21.593
We started cooking it, it was freebasing.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.473
And now it's just fake.

00:02:26.473 --> 00:02:31.345
Fake stuff that everybody's addicted to.

00:02:31.345 --> 00:02:32.480
But I don't really like getting high,

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:33.973
It's not fun anymore.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:36.333
It's maintenance.

00:02:38.830 --> 00:02:40.680
Back East, we used to go camping,

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:42.383
over here it's called survival.

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.650
And they used to call
us white trailer trash,

00:02:46.650 --> 00:02:48.763
and now I say trailer trash wannabe.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.460
I would love to have my big trailer

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:53.713
we used to go camping in.

00:02:54.720 --> 00:02:56.833
I can live there all year long.

00:03:00.699 --> 00:03:03.813
I just gotta get myself
together and go to rehab

00:03:07.007 --> 00:03:07.957
and start all over.

00:03:08.810 --> 00:03:11.080
- [Mark] So your son is how old now?

00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:14.985
- My son was born in 1987.

00:03:14.985 --> 00:03:17.870
He's 33.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.253
- [Mark] You raised him
for part of his life?

00:03:20.253 --> 00:03:21.253
- Until he was nine.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.220
- [Mark] That's when the
drugs kind of took hold?

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:29.220
- [Helia] Yeah, his dad
kept him home from school,

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:33.420
and then the state came in

00:03:33.420 --> 00:03:37.980
and he was drinking
and drug paraphernalia.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:39.960
He let this Brazilian lady in

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:45.860
and after that I couldn't leave the dad.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.600
But I was working and I
could pass a drug test

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:49.753
but his dad couldn't.

00:03:52.179 --> 00:03:53.760
So they were about to take my son.

00:03:53.760 --> 00:03:55.820
So I called Debbie, his aunt,

00:03:55.820 --> 00:03:59.750
and she took temporary custody of him.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.503
And she brought him up
right, he went to college.

00:04:06.956 --> 00:04:10.770
I'm like 75% sure that if I would have

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:12.867
brought him out here with me,

00:04:12.867 --> 00:04:14.217
he'd end up on the streets.

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:19.810
Being with her, he went to college.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:21.040
He doesn't do drugs.

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:23.993
He drinks now because
dad died two years ago,

00:04:25.585 --> 00:04:27.270
but still a truck driver.

00:04:27.270 --> 00:04:31.040
He drives an 18-wheeler and I'm proud.

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:33.050
I talk to him on the phone now

00:04:34.929 --> 00:04:37.570
and it's just good to have family back.

00:04:37.570 --> 00:04:39.280
- [Mark] It's good that he's
not living on the streets.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.710
- [Helia] Yeah, yeah, yeah. He's smart.

00:04:41.710 --> 00:04:46.540
He's going to work and I'm just glad that,

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.530
I mean I missed him all
these years and stuff,

00:04:48.530 --> 00:04:51.683
but I'm glad that he was brought up right.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:54.899
- [Mark] How do you support
yourself living here?

00:04:54.899 --> 00:04:59.899
- I got food stamps, GA,
hustling the streets,

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:10.910
shoplifting, mostly I do distraction.

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.900
Like I'll go in and knock down shelves

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:17.370
and my friends get to it.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:22.370
It's not right, but it is what it is.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.070
- [Mark] What do you think
people that don't do drugs

00:05:26.070 --> 00:05:28.310
that watch these kind of
videos, watch these stories,

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:30.123
don't understand about addiction?

00:05:31.630 --> 00:05:36.630
- They don't, unless you've
been there, you have no idea.

00:05:38.720 --> 00:05:40.600
It's just sad.

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:42.150
I tell the kids,

00:05:42.150 --> 00:05:44.010
I say, "Go to school, do your homework,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.130
listen to your parents, don't drink,

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:49.230
don't do drugs, go to
college, get a degree,

00:05:49.230 --> 00:05:53.007
don't end up like these people
sleeping on the street."

00:05:55.099 --> 00:05:59.150
And I just hope that maybe
just five out of a hundred

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:01.987
make it to college just
because they heard,

00:06:01.987 --> 00:06:04.697
"Hey, who's that crazy lady saying that?"

00:06:08.940 --> 00:06:11.420
If you just live right and go to college

00:06:11.420 --> 00:06:15.260
and get a degree and don't
do drugs, you got it made.

00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:22.380
If you don't, you fall
into alcohol and drugs.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:27.223
It pretty much takes a lot
of years out of your life.

00:06:29.040 --> 00:06:30.870
- [Mark] How do you think this lifestyle

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.653
has changed you over the years?

00:06:36.800 --> 00:06:37.913
- Made me numb.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.210
I gotta drink and do
drugs just to become numb

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.270
and made me tougher,

00:06:46.548 --> 00:06:48.743
like I'm pretty much fearless,

00:06:50.169 --> 00:06:53.040
like I go out there at two,
three o'clock in the morning

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.790
just like in the middle of the afternoon

00:06:57.466 --> 00:06:59.503
and somebody like me
shouldn't really be out there

00:06:59.503 --> 00:07:02.640
with all the pro creatures, I call them.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.170
I consider myself pretty street smart

00:07:14.170 --> 00:07:16.863
which is nothing to be proud about.

00:07:18.152 --> 00:07:20.500
But you learn how to survive

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.930
and you learn who the gang members are,

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:28.180
you learn who like the OGs, the top guys,

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:30.540
and you learn how they
are and who they are,

00:07:30.540 --> 00:07:32.110
and then you start hanging with them

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.960
and you're pretty much protected

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:37.050
because they'll say, "Don't mess with her.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:38.140
She's like one of us."

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:39.810
But I don't belong to no gang.

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:41.913
I'm just me on one team.

00:07:44.550 --> 00:07:45.580
- [Mark] What would you
say to a young person

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.680
who's considering going
down this kind of path?

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:49.513
- Oh man.

00:07:50.425 --> 00:07:52.833
I hate seeing the girls half my age.

00:07:57.040 --> 00:07:58.383
Just don't do it.

00:08:00.010 --> 00:08:02.983
Don't fall because once you
fall, it's hard to get up.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:08.153
But I see a lot of them walking with,

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.720
I know where they're going,
who they're going with,

00:08:12.720 --> 00:08:13.700
what they're going to do,

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:16.500
and how they're going to feel afterwards.

00:08:16.500 --> 00:08:18.860
But I really can't do nothing about it

00:08:18.860 --> 00:08:23.103
because I have to walk
around on these streets.

00:08:25.545 --> 00:08:28.410
It's sad, but a lot of times,

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:31.040
I'll say, "Your mom just
paid me $50 to come get you.

00:08:31.040 --> 00:08:31.970
You got to come with me

00:08:31.970 --> 00:08:33.590
and she's going to give me another $50."

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:35.900
And it's all just a lie
just to get them away

00:08:35.900 --> 00:08:37.713
from whoever they're with.

00:08:39.860 --> 00:08:44.070
The other day my little
friend was getting into a car

00:08:44.070 --> 00:08:45.510
and it was undercover cop.

00:08:45.510 --> 00:08:47.943
And right before she got in, I grabbed her

00:08:47.943 --> 00:08:50.670
and I'm like, "Your mom
wants you, come with me."

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:52.393
And she was mad.

00:08:52.393 --> 00:08:56.560
But once she knew that he was police,

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:57.943
then she loved me.

00:08:59.010 --> 00:09:03.110
And I go around saving
these little youngsters,

00:09:03.110 --> 00:09:04.300
they're smoking fentanyl,

00:09:04.300 --> 00:09:06.993
and they're just dying like flies.

00:09:07.960 --> 00:09:11.560
Like I walked by and these little kids

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:14.070
turning blue and nobody's even,

00:09:14.070 --> 00:09:18.160
like everybody's just walking
by and not even acknowledged.

00:09:18.160 --> 00:09:19.810
It's just another homeless people,

00:09:19.810 --> 00:09:23.823
but it's somebody's son,
it's somebody's daughter.

00:09:24.770 --> 00:09:29.043
I carry my purse with Narcan.

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.000
Just last month I saved five of them.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:35.610
And it's funny because
after you save them,

00:09:35.610 --> 00:09:37.240
you give them this Narcan,

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:41.090
they can't get high for 72 hours,

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:42.690
so they get so mad.

00:09:42.690 --> 00:09:46.620
It's like, bitch you're mad
at me for saving your life?

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.380
They don't understand
until this one little girl,

00:09:50.380 --> 00:09:53.160
she went to jail and she had
been there for six months,

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:54.600
and then I ended up in there

00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:58.280
and she's like, "Oh, Boston, I
love you. You saved my life."

00:09:58.280 --> 00:09:59.530
But like for the whole time

00:09:59.530 --> 00:10:01.753
that she was on the street, she was mad.

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:07.023
You don't really realize
until the smoke clears.

00:10:08.580 --> 00:10:10.340
Lot of times when I go to jail,

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.930
three, four days, over
the weekend and stuff,

00:10:12.930 --> 00:10:14.650
the smoke clears.

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:15.860
And when I come out,

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:17.370
I go straight to the Woman's Place

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:20.180
and I want to go upstairs to rehab.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.990
But they say, "No, come back tomorrow."

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:27.000
And I know that if I
leave, I'll just smoke.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:28.670
And then I won't be back tomorrow.

00:10:28.670 --> 00:10:30.590
But the last three times,

00:10:30.590 --> 00:10:32.590
they actually had to call the police,

00:10:32.590 --> 00:10:35.142
and it was funny because the police,

00:10:35.142 --> 00:10:39.683
I give them a hard time and
I'm kind of wise when I drink,

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:44.407
and police were like, "Please,
please keep her there."

00:10:46.733 --> 00:10:50.130
And just once I go back
out there, it's over.

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:53.770
- [Mark] What's one of
the most horrible things

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.633
you've seen down here in the Tenderloin?

00:10:57.630 --> 00:11:01.183
- Pretty much, my best friend
getting stabbed to death.

00:11:02.350 --> 00:11:04.450
And there was nothing I could do about it.

00:11:06.350 --> 00:11:09.310
And then police wanted me to tell on

00:11:09.310 --> 00:11:11.227
the people that stabbed him,

00:11:14.046 --> 00:11:16.030
but once you snitch on those guys,

00:11:16.030 --> 00:11:21.030
you pretty much either have
to leave or end up dead.

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:23.070
So they wanted me to point them out,

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:26.060
but half of them like went
back to their own country.

00:11:26.060 --> 00:11:27.363
Drug dealers and stuff.

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:35.420
It was pretty bad because after
he couldn't breathe anymore,

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:36.900
I was in that circle,

00:11:36.900 --> 00:11:39.510
and I got weak, like, Oh my God,

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:41.910
cause they will kill you
just so you don't talk.

00:11:43.060 --> 00:11:46.293
But I got strength and I just ran.

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:52.760
After that, it was pretty
much just suffering it out.

00:11:54.290 --> 00:11:58.313
It was my best friend and now he's gone,

00:12:00.317 --> 00:12:01.683
but it is what it is.

00:12:05.316 --> 00:12:08.670
- [Mark] Do you have regrets
about any parts of your life?

00:12:08.670 --> 00:12:09.503
- Yeah.

00:12:12.740 --> 00:12:16.030
I wish I didn't keep my family

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:18.110
worried about me for 20 years,

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.733
but there's nothing I
can do about that now.

00:12:21.875 --> 00:12:23.220
But I just make it up to them

00:12:23.220 --> 00:12:27.010
by visiting when they want to visit

00:12:29.474 --> 00:12:33.703
and calling them all the time
and just keeping in touch.

00:12:36.340 --> 00:12:39.913
That's all they want is
for me to be all right.

00:12:42.708 --> 00:12:43.541
- [Mark] All right Helia,

00:12:43.541 --> 00:12:45.311
thank you so much for talking with me.

00:12:45.311 --> 00:12:46.144
- Thank you.

00:12:46.144 --> 00:12:47.420
- [Mark] Good luck with
whatever you do next.

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:48.410
- Yeah.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:49.310
- [Mark] Thanks.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:50.143
- Thank you.

00:13:01.929 --> 00:13:02.850
- [Mark] That was great.

00:13:02.850 --> 00:13:03.683
- Thank you.

00:13:03.683 --> 00:13:04.963
- [Mark] You're a beautiful speaker.

